---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Andrew Mata — PhD Candidate">
  <section class="hero section" id="about">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1>Andrew Mata</h1>
        <p class="hero-role">PhD Candidate in Computer Science</p>
        <p class="hero-affiliation">
          Stony Brook University
        </p>
        <p class="hero-bio">
          I am a PhD candidate in the <a href="https://stanleybak.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reliable Systems Lab</a>
          under the supervision of Dr. Stanley Bak. My research focuses on AI safety and
          robustness of reinforcement learning agents and other learning-enabled systems. I develop
          methods for adversarial evaluation, robustness certification, and systematic discovery
          of failure modes in machine learning systems.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <a href="mailto:andrew.c.mata@gmail.com">Email</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/andrewmata13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrew-mata-56697740a/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=q1qF0jwAAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-photo">
        <img src="/images/headshot.JPG" alt="Andrew Mata" class="headshot" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="projects">
    <h2>Selected Projects</h2>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Zero-One Attack: Adversarial Evaluation of RL Controllers <a href="https://github.com/andrewmata13/Zero-OneAttack" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pub-link">(code)</a></h3>
      <p>
        A framework for generating worst-case perturbations in both observation space and activation timing
        to systematically evaluate the robustness of reinforcement learning agents. Designed state-time
        perturbation attacks that degraded closed-loop neural controllers by 195% more than prior attacks
        across 4 complex MuJoCo control benchmarks. Won Best Artifact Evaluation Package Award at ICCPS 2024.
      </p>
      <div class="project-gifs">
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/clean.gif" alt="Agent performing normally without attack" />
          <figcaption>Clean</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/zero_one_attack.gif" alt="Agent degraded under Zero-One Attack" />
          <figcaption>Zero-One Attack</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="project-tags">
        <span class="tag">Python</span>
        <span class="tag">PyTorch</span>
        <span class="tag">MuJoCo</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Symbolic Gaussian Smoothing <a href="https://github.com/andrewmata13/Deterministic_Smoothing" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pub-link">(code)</a></h3>
      <p>
        A deterministic robustness certification method that replaces Monte Carlo randomized smoothing with
        symbolic moment propagation, enabling analytical computation of output distribution statistics
        in a single forward pass. Provides scalable robustness guarantees without stochastic sampling.
      </p>
      <div class="project-gifs">
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/noise_figure-1.png" alt="Symbolic Gaussian smoothing noise propagation" />
          <figcaption>MNIST and F-MNIST</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="project-tags">
        <span class="tag">Python</span>
        <span class="tag">PyTorch</span>
        <span class="tag">Neural Network Verification</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>RS Certified Switcher <a href="https://github.com/andrewmata13/RL_Switcher" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pub-link">(code)</a></h3>
      <p>
        A runtime-certified binary switcher for adversarial robustness in reinforcement learning.
        At each step, the system chooses between a high-performance PPO policy and a safe backup controller.
        A binary switcher certified with symbolic smoothing detects adversarial observations and triggers
        the backup, supporting repeated and multi-burst attacks while maintaining near-clean performance.
      </p>
      <div class="project-gifs">
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/cert_collapse-1.png" alt="Attack detection via certified switcher" />
          <figcaption>Attack Detection</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="project-tags">
        <span class="tag">Python</span>
        <span class="tag">PyTorch</span>
        <span class="tag">Reinforcement Learning</span>
        <span class="tag">MuJoCo</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project">
      <h3>Koopman Surrogate Falsification (FReaK) <a href="https://github.com/Abdu-Hekal/FReaK" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pub-link">(code)</a></h3>
      <p>
        A scalable framework for discovering failure cases in controllers using Koopman-based surrogate models
        combined with reachability analysis and MILP encodings of Signal Temporal Logic specifications.
        Outperformed competing tools in 16 of 19 benchmarks in the 2022 ARCH falsification competition.
      </p>
      <div class="project-tags">
        <span class="tag">MATLAB</span>
        <span class="tag">MILP Optimization</span>
        <span class="tag">Reachability Analysis</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

